    skos:definition "a small seedless variety of the grape, largely consumed for confectionery and culinary purposes. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 129]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated fields — definition use: Customs currants are dried Corinth grapes (imported in cwt from Greece, the Ionian Islands, Turkey), not Ribes garden currants. | source_taxon remove: Customs currants are dried grapes, not Ribes. | source_taxon remove: Customs currants are dried grapes, not Ribes. | source_taxon add: Currants = dried Corinth grapes (Simmonds 1892 s.v. CURRANTS)."@en ;
